From: Benjamin Bruun <bb@onomondo.com>
Subject: [PATCH] constraints: allow compiling out the constraint messages

ASN__CTFAIL only null-checks its callback at runtime, so every
_constraint() still linked (the skeleton BIT STRING, OID and string checks
the descriptors point at) keeps its format string, __FILE__ literal and
td->name reference in rodata although nothing ever passes a callback.
ASN_DISABLE_CONSTRAINT_MSG swallows the whole call.
---
diff --git a/src/ipa/libasn/constraints.h b/src/ipa/libasn/constraints.h
--- a/src/ipa/libasn/constraints.h
+++ b/src/ipa/libasn/constraints.h
@@ -53,7 +53,14 @@
 /*
  * Invoke the callback with a complete error message.
  */
+#ifdef	ASN_DISABLE_CONSTRAINT_MSG
+/* Swallows the call and its arguments: the format strings, __FILE__ literals
+ * and td->name references in the skeleton _constraint() bodies vanish from
+ * the image. Nothing in this codebase ever passes a ctfailcb. */
+#define	ASN__CTFAIL(...)	do{}while(0)
+#else
 #define	ASN__CTFAIL	if(ctfailcb) ctfailcb
+#endif
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
